From fa0a4efd141466873a87a8b0b54b0dfea6c82816 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaseduardo1656 <lucas@MacBook-Pro-de-lucas.local>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:28:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Choose host RPS frequency from RC6 busyness (#176)

Without GuC (-disablegfxfirmware) Apple's requested/boost fields stay at
RP0 and the native usage values are zero, so the host pmNotify answer
pinned the GT at its maximum frequency (observed 1200 MHz constantly on
ADL-P 0x46A8 while RC6 residency was ~90%).

Derive the answer from GT busyness instead: the complement of RC6
residency (GEN6_GT_GFX_RC6, already read by the power sampler from the
always-accessible mirror range), evaluated over >=16 ms windows. Jump to
RP0 at >=90% busy, step up at >=70%, step down below 30%, and restart at
RPn after a 100 ms callback gap. No forcewake, MMIO writes or busy-wait
sampling in the callback. -wex-hostrps-max keeps the previous answer.

The policy is header-only and covered by a CPU test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
